## 7. Placement checklist

- [ ] Disclosure appears before or at the first interaction, not only in a settings page
- [ ] Disclosure is legible on mobile, and not hidden behind a tooltip or expander
- [ ] Disclosure survives deep links that skip the landing page
- [ ] Voice or telephony channels carry an audible equivalent
- [ ] Embedded or white-labelled instances of the assistant carry it too
- [ ] Route to a human is stated, and works
- [ ] Machine-readable marking decided per output channel, not just for the chat UI
- [ ] Wording reviewed by whoever signs off legal and user-facing copy

